! muon_gun.cmnd
! Muon CALIBRATION sample: J/psi -> mu mu  +  Z -> mu mu resonance gun for the CMS
! full-simulation pseudodata generator (parnassus.torch_delphes.generate_pseudodata
! --process muongun).
!
! PURPOSE
!   The shipped qcd_dijet.cmnd sample contains very few muons. That starves the
!   muon parameters of CMSEnergyFlowDefault:
!     MuonTrackingEfficiency.eff_logits[0..5]     6 (|eta|, pt) regions
!     MuonMomentumSmearing.resolution_module.{a,b,scale}_raw[0..2]
!
! WHY RESONANCES (not a continuous single-muon spectrum, not pT lines)
!   The muon smearing is log-normal in pT: in ln(pT) it is a shift (per-region
!   scale) plus a Gaussian convolution of width sqrt(a^2 + (b*pT)^2). Any SMOOTH
!   single-muon spectrum (flat-in-log, power law, ...) is invariant under the
!   convolution away from its edges, so a_raw / low-pT b_raw leave the reco pT
!   marginal unchanged and cannot be fitted from it (measured: gradient SNR
!   < 0.5 per batch for every smooth spectrum; see
!   .claude/docs/muon_gun_lines_eta_split_plan.md). What carries the width is a
!   feature sharper than the resolution -- a resonance mass peak, which is
!   physical: its width IS the resolution, its position the scale. The tuning
!   loss therefore forms the pair mass of the two leading muons per event
!   (per |eta|-region pair) and this file throws exactly ONE resonance per event
!   so that pair is unambiguous. scale_raw needs no special spectrum (the
!   quantile-W2 sees a shift at full strength once the shape terms are split by
!   |eta| region); eff_logits come from the per-region count terms as before.
!
!   J/psi (m = 3.097 GeV): soft daughters (~0.3-10 GeV) -> populate the eff bin
!     (0.1, 1] and give the low-pT (a-dominated) mass peak.
!   Z (m = 91.19 GeV, window 70-110 GeV): daughters ~20-250 GeV -> a in every
!     region, some b lever from the boosted tail (b*pT >~ a above ~100 GeV),
!     the (1, 1000] eff bins. There are NO muons above 1 TeV: eff_logits[2,5]
!     and rate_raw stay pinned at their defaults on both sides.
!
! COVERAGE (see the region binning in learnable.py CMS_EFF_REGION_SPECS)
!   Muon efficiency regions: |eta| bins [0, 1.5] and (1.5, 2.5];
!                            pt bins (0.1, 1], (1, 1000], (1000, inf).
!   Muon smearing regions:   |eta| bins [0, 0.5], (0.5, 1.5], (1.5, 2.5].
!   Parents uniform in eta in [-2.5, 2.5]; daughters of soft J/psi spread beyond
!   that (out of every region -> simply not reconstructed).
!
! NOTES
!   * The Gun:* keys are NOT Pythia settings: parnassus.pythia.HepMC3Generator's
!     single-job driver parses and STRIPS them before handing the rest of this
!     file to Pythia's readFile(). Everything else here is ordinary Pythia -- in
!     particular the decay-channel settings below are what turn the thrown
!     parents into mu+ mu- pairs (the driver appends each parent with status 1
!     and its mass from ParticleData::mSel, then pythia.next() decays it; QED
!     FSR photons off the muons appear and are physical).
!   * ONE parent per event (Gun:nPerEvent = 1) -- required by the leading-2
!     pair-mass rule of the loss.
!   * Gun events contain ONLY the decay products (plus FSR photons) -- no
!     underlying event. Use this to fit the muon block; the other species'
!     terms are empty (graph-connected zeros).
!   * Do NOT set Random:seed here. The per-worker seed is injected by the
!     driver before this file is read, and it also drives the gun sampling.
!   * generate_pseudodata.py injects --pt-hat-min only for the dijet process by
!     default (there is no hard process to cut on here).

! ---- Gun definition (consumed by the driver, stripped before Pythia) ----
Gun:on = on
Gun:ids = 443 23                    ! J/psi and Z, one of them per event (uniform)
Gun:nPerEvent = 1
Gun:pTmin = 1. 1.                   ! GeV, per id (J/psi, Z)
Gun:pTmax = 500. 500.               ! GeV, per id
Gun:pTpower = 1.5                   ! dN/dpT ~ pT^-1.5 (falling)
Gun:etaMin = -2.5
Gun:etaMax = 2.5

! ---- Decays: force the mu+ mu- channels (ordinary Pythia settings) ----
443:onMode = off
443:onIfMatch = 13 -13
23:onMode = off
23:onIfAny = 13
23:mMin = 70.                       ! Z line shape window (kills the Breit-Wigner tail)
23:mMax = 110.

! ---- Pythia: no hard process, we fill the event record ourselves ----
ProcessLevel:all = off
Beams:idA = 2212
Beams:idB = 2212
Beams:eCM = 13000.                  ! only sets the bookkeeping beam particles

! ---- Suppress per-event and initialization printout ----
Next:numberShowInfo = 0
Next:numberShowProcess = 0
Next:numberShowEvent = 0
Init:showProcesses = off
Init:showMultipartonInteractions = off
Init:showChangedSettings = off
Init:showChangedParticleData = off
Stat:showProcessLevel = off
Stat:showPartonLevel = off
Stat:showErrors = off
